"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2c8d35969f7ccaf5b74ac1ac6fc5fcd4c79aea50268a8bd8d3ff2e4201fad256","event_uuid":"a5223011-4872-462e-8458-d9a67c89934f","position":{"commit_sha":"7a2dc2b2b480bc939c97495c5ae41e18e6196be9","position":"1785780629874644001-a5223011-4872-462e-8458-d9a67c89934f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785640134259404001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ce92ed95-faa7-48f6-845d-29e3cd54e0df","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0fa6-3c0b-d90b-43f4"},{"link_uuid":"85351f4c-1fc5-4e24-be9c-a28ec6b4994d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"347d-48f0-f634-4cd7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAutomated bug filers can spam duplicates, file on single flakes, or silently break when create args/gates change (0e15/376d class: gate changes broke automated surfaces). The audit surface is the THREE existing filers — no new filer is built; this ticket HARDENS what exists and documents the contract for future filers: the heartbeat-alert filer (scripts/canary_bridge.py cmd_heartbeat_alert ~:197) and the binding-drift-alert filer (cmd_binding_drift_alert ~:350) — canary_bridge.py has exactly these two create sites, verified by inventory —, plus `_file_conflict_bug_ticket` in the reconciler applier (src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py:135, called at :522), which today files one bug per unresolved (local, Jira) conflict with no dedup key, no template contract, and no empty-detail abort.\n\n## Approach\nPer OSS practice (PyTorch DISABLED-test bot, Flutter flake bot, Sentry fingerprinting, Alertmanager 'for:'): dedup via a stable per-check TAG searched with has-tag (one open ticket per check); file only after N>=2 consecutive reds; max one accumulation comment/day; templated body (check name, first-red time, run URL, failing-output tail, workflow path) with abort-if-empty-detail; recovery comment on green with close left to agents is documented in the CONTRACT as the default for future filers whose bugs carry investigation value; it is NOT retrofitted anywhere in this ticket. The two canary_bridge filers ALREADY auto-close their alert ticket on green via `rebar transition open closed --force-close` (cmd_heartbeat_alert ~:247-262, cmd_binding_drift_alert ~:398-410) — that existing recovery contract is KEPT AS-IS (pure state alerts, nothing to investigate once green); the audit records this divergence and its rationale in the table rather than retrofitting agent-close onto them. Pattern elements apply per-site by SEMANTIC FIT, recorded in the audit table: the N>=2 consecutive-red threshold applies only where a derivable red/green run signal exists: the HEARTBEAT filer only — its stale check fails the canary run (the 'Fail job on stale' step), so the workflow's previous run conclusion carries the signal. The BINDING-DRIFT filer gets NO threshold, with rationale recorded: its oracle never fails the run (conclusion carries no drift signal), and drift is PERSISTENT state, not a flake — it cannot self-heal between runs, so first-observation filing is correct and dedup + daily accumulation already bound spam; the conflict filer has no cycle semantics, so it gets dedup (stable tag derived from the conflict identity: local id + jira key), template, abort-if-empty, and detected_by — not the threshold. CONSECUTIVE-RED STATE STORE: no new state store — the workflow's own run history is the durable state. On red, the filer queries the same workflow's previous completed run conclusion (gh api repos/{repo}/actions/workflows/{file}/runs?status=completed&per_page=2, excluding the current run); previous-also-red => threshold met; previous-green-or-absent => first red, no ticket. Dedup search runs FIRST: an existing open tagged ticket always takes the accumulate-comment path regardless of threshold. ACCUMULATION DEDUP ('max one accumulation comment/day'): derived from the target ticket's OWN comment history — the accumulation comment opens with a stable marker line; the filer reads the ticket (rebar show --output json), finds the newest marker-bearing comment, and skips if it is <24h old. The ticket store IS the durable state; no new store, and the */20 cron cannot spam. First-red time in the template = the previous red run's timestamp. WORKFLOW THREADING (scope): the consuming alert steps in .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml today pass only STALE/RUN_URL/DRIFT_* env; the heartbeat alert step's run-history query additionally needs GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }} (already used by other steps in that workflow), the repo (github.repository), and the workflow file id (the literal filename) threaded as step env — enumerated as workflow edits in scope, heartbeat step only. The contract doc records the same recipe for future filers with run-conclusion signals. LIFECYCLE: green with no open tagged ticket (single flake that never crossed the threshold) => recovery path no-ops on the empty has-tag search — stated as an invariant and unit-tested. USER-REQUIRED ADDITIONS: (a) audit ALL existing auto-bug-creation sites and retrofit the fitting pattern elements; (b) document the bug-creation contract for automation — exact rebar create args, exit codes, dedup search command, REBAR_DETECTED_BY env var — so auto-filers always fire a well-formed create.\n\n## Scope\n- canary/heartbeat/binding-drift filer scripts or workflow logic (coordinate with Tier-3 migration child if concurrent)\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py `_file_conflict_bug_ticket`: dedup tag + template + abort-if-empty + detected_by (no threshold — no red/green cycle)\n- docs: bug-creation contract page\n- audit table of every auto-file site in the change description, with a per-site row: which pattern elements apply and why\n\n## Testing\nHeartbeat-filer unit tests: first red -> no ticket; second consecutive red -> one ticket with template fields; third red same day -> accumulation comment, not a new ticket; second accumulation within 24h -> skipped (marker-line dedup); green with open ticket -> existing auto-close path preserved (transition open closed --force-close, unchanged); green with NO open ticket -> no-op, exit 0; empty detail -> abort with loud log, no hollow ticket; previous-run query failure -> treated as first red (fail toward not filing, loud log). Binding-drift tests: first observed drift -> one ticket (no threshold, rationale in table); repeat drift -> accumulation not duplicate; green -> existing auto-close preserved. Conflict-filer tests: same conflict twice -> one ticket + one accumulation comment; distinct conflicts -> distinct tickets; empty conflict detail -> abort.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All three audited auto-file sites use the fitting dedup+template pattern elements (audit table enumerates sites x elements with rationale, including the kept auto-close divergence and the binding-drift no-threshold rationale).\n- [ ] Heartbeat consecutive-red threshold implemented via workflow run-history query; no new state store introduced; single flake files nothing.\n- [ ] Bug-creation contract documented and referenced by every filer.\n- [ ] Filer behavior covered by the unit tests above, including the green-with-no-ticket no-op and the query-failure arm.\n- [ ] detected_by stamped by all automated filers (env var from the detected-by child).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml","reason":"dedup+threshold filer logic"},{"path":"docs/","reason":"bug-creation contract page"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"],["relates_to","0fa6-3c0b-d90b-43f4"],["relates_to","347d-48f0-f634-4cd7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","parent_status_uuid":"cfd47675-1c7b-42b3-b03b-4cf30b235d44","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["canary","automation"],"ticket_id":"4527-0cfa-d31a-4a08","ticket_type":"story","title":"Auto-bug-filer hardening: dedup pattern, all-site audit, contract doc","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["af4c4eb4-1973-4700-a2bc-b2a0eb8697f4","832cc223-cab7-4b18-bc9c-9e97c7577db1","466c8c95-8d6a-45a7-b0f5-333bf00e823a","ef4d54ab-8aae-4339-883c-1e08be727586","3db7482b-f061-4404-b256-53d9dba0b4d1","31411c63-7758-4459-8694-431265967553","2b37a89a-5870-4641-9005-94a243e88b44","cfd47675-1c7b-42b3-b03b-4cf30b235d44","a5223011-4872-462e-8458-d9a67c89934f","ce92ed95-faa7-48f6-845d-29e3cd54e0df","85351f4c-1fc5-4e24-be9c-a28ec6b4994d"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785801521038281371,"uuid":"1bb50273-7a15-4e2a-9c58-d8b990bd3220"}